# 17. What is a Text Editor?

A text editor is a program used to create and modify text files.

Linux provides many text editors.

Common examples:

```text
nano
vim
vi
emacs
```

Text editors are used for:

* Writing scripts
* Editing configuration files
* Editing source code
* Modifying system files
* Creating notes
* Editing logs
* Writing shell scripts

