# 18. What is Vim?

Vim stands for:

```text
Vi Improved
```

Vim is a powerful command-line text editor.

It is an improved version of the traditional Unix `vi` editor.

Vim is commonly available on Linux systems.

---

# 19. Why Learn Vim?

Vim is useful because:

* It works from the terminal.
* It is lightweight.
* It is powerful.
* It can edit large files.
* It provides keyboard-based navigation.
* It provides powerful search features.
* It can be used remotely through SSH.
* It is commonly available on Linux systems.

For cybersecurity and system administration, knowing Vim is useful when working on remote Linux machines where graphical editors may not be available.

