# 37. Vim Search Patterns

Vim supports patterns and regular expressions.

For example:

```text
/error
```

searches for error.

You can also use patterns such as:

```text
/^ERROR
```

This searches for lines beginning with `ERROR`.

Example:

```text
/^ERROR
```

---

# 38. Searching for Numbers

You can search for numbers using:

```text
/[0-9]
```

This finds a digit.

For example:

```text
/[0-9][0-9][0-9]
```

can search for three consecutive digits.

---

# 39. Vim Search Case Sensitivity

Searches are normally case-sensitive depending on Vim settings.

You can use:

```text
:set ignorecase
```

to ignore case.

Example:

```text
:set ignorecase
```

Now searching:

```text
/error
```

can match:

```text
error
ERROR
Error
```

To return to case-sensitive searching:

```text
:set noignorecase
```

